    "focal_pair": {
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 4 USER]\ne029\tThat sounds more abstract than the actual relationship.\ne030\tTomas found and protected most of these boxes when our grandmother's apartment was cleared.\ne031\tHe feels he took responsibility while I now act like the archive belongs to a process I control.\ne032\tI did spend hundreds of hours organizing it, but I joined later.\ne033\tIf I insist on a catalog-first approach, he may hear that his years of care count less because they were not systematic.\n[Turn 4 ASSISTANT]\ne034\tThe labor histories matter.\ne035\tFormal organization can accidentally become a claim to authority, just as physical custody and early rescue can become one.\ne036\tYou may need to recognize those contributions explicitly before negotiating the exhibition, not because recognition settles final say but because otherwise each procedural disagreement carries an older argument about ownership.\ne037\tA shared decision process will feel hollow if either of you believes the other's kind of care is treated as secondary.",
